{
  "sn55.27:0.1": "Linked Discourses 55.27 ",
  "sn55.27:0.2": "3. About Sarakāni ",
  "sn55.27:0.3": "With Anāthapiṇḍika (2nd) ",
  "sn55.27:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn55.27:1.2": "Now at that time the householder Anāthapiṇḍika was sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "sn55.27:1.3": "Then he addressed a man, ",
  "sn55.27:1.4": "“Please, my man, go to Venerable Ānanda, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Say to him: ",
  "sn55.27:1.5": "‘Sir, the householder Anāthapiṇḍika is sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "sn55.27:1.6": "He bows with his head to your feet.’ ",
  "sn55.27:1.7": "And then say: ",
  "sn55.27:1.8": "‘Sir, please visit him at his home out of sympathy.’” ",
  "sn55.27:2.1": "“Yes, sir,” that man replied. He did as Anāthapiṇḍika asked. ",
  "sn55.27:2.2": "",
  "sn55.27:2.3": "",
  "sn55.27:2.4": "",
  "sn55.27:2.5": "",
  "sn55.27:2.6": "Ānanda consented with silence. ",
  "sn55.27:3.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to the home of the householder Anāthapiṇḍika. He sat down on the seat spread out and said to Anāthapiṇḍika, ",
  "sn55.27:3.2": "“I hope you’re keeping well, householder, I hope you’re all right. I hope your pain is fading, not growing; that its fading is evident, not its growing.” ",
  "sn55.27:3.3": "“Sir, I’m not keeping well, I’m not getting by. My pain is terrible and growing, not fading; its growing is evident, not its fading.” ",
  "sn55.27:4.1":